+# Working day to day with Rojo
+
+Git is the source of truth for this game. Code lives in files under `src/`, and `rojo serve`
+syncs those files into your own dev place in Studio. The place is a build of the repo, so it is
+never the master copy. The Layout table in the [README](../README.md) shows which folder
+becomes which instance.
+
+## Setup (once)
+
+1. Install the tools: `rokit install` (from `rokit.toml`).
+2. Install the packages: `pesde install`. Run it again in `test_packages/` for Jest. Do this
+   again whenever `pesde.toml` or `pesde.lock` changes, including after a pull.
+3. Make your own dev place: publish a copy of the place to your own account or group. Never
+   serve into a shared or live place.
+4. Add your dev place id to `servePlaceIds` in `default.project.json` (in your own change, or
+   locally). Rojo then refuses to sync into any other place.
+
+## Daily loop
+
+1. Pull `main` and create your branch. Stop `rojo serve` first: a checkout, pull, rebase, stash,
+   or `pesde install` rewrites many watched files at once, and Rojo can crash on that.
+2. Start `rojo serve` from the repo root (port 34872). In Studio, open your dev place and click
+   **Connect** in the Rojo plugin.
+3. Edit files in your editor. Each save syncs into Studio.
+4. Use Studio to look, playtest, and run the Jest specs (`ServerScriptService.Tests.Specs`).
+5. Before you push, run the checks in the README (`rojo sourcemap`, `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene`,
+   `stylua --check`). Then read `git status` and `git diff`: they should show only the files you
+   meant to change.
+
+## Where changes go
+
+| You want to... | Do it in |
+|---|---|
+| Change a script or module | Its `.luau` file under `src/` |
+| Add a Script, LocalScript, or ModuleScript | A new file in the right `src/` folder (`.server.luau`, `.client.luau`, `.luau`) |
+| Add a spec | `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs/<Name>.spec.luau` |
+| Set attributes or tags on a synced instance | A `<Name>.meta.json` beside the file (`init.meta.json` for a folder) |
+| Add a library | `pesde.toml`, then `pesde install`. Never edit `roblox_packages/` |
+| Change how folders map into the place | `default.project.json`. See the last section |
+
+**Don't edit synced instances in Studio.** A script edit, property, attribute, or new child made
+in Studio under a synced folder is overwritten by the next sync, and Git never sees it. If you
+built something real in Studio (a model or GUI), export it into the repo as an `.rbxm`
+(**Save to File**) and commit that.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Studio still receives changes.** Rojo 7.7.0 and 7.7.1 can crash when a file or folder is
+  deleted, moved, or renamed while serving. After you do any of those, look at the terminal for
+  `Rojo crashed!`. If it stopped, restart `rojo serve` and click **Connect** again.
+- **The new code arrived before you test.** Open the script in Studio and confirm your edit is
+  there. If an error's line number didn't move with your edit, you are still running old code.
+- **You're connected to the right place and branch.** The place runs whatever the connected
+  server's folder has checked out. A merged pull request changes nothing there until you pull.
+- **One server per place.** If you use a second worktree, give it its own port
+  (`rojo serve --port <port>`). Point the plugin at only one server at a time.
+
+## Keeping `default.project.json` healthy
+
+This file maps every folder into the place. A bad merge here breaks sync, the sourcemap, type
+checking, and Jest for everyone.
+
+- **The README's Layout table is the spec.** Any change to a mount updates the table in the same
+  pull request.
+- **Resolve conflicts by hand against the table.** Don't take "both sides" blindly. Things to
+  watch for:
+  - Duplicated nodes, such as `TestPackages` landing in `ReplicatedStorage`. Test packages go in
+    `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`.
+  - Typos in `$path`, such as `StarterPlayerScript` for `StarterPlayerScripts`. A `$path`
+    that doesn't exist makes `rojo serve` and `rojo sourcemap` fail.
+  - Dropped settings, such as `globIgnorePaths`. It stops `src/ServerScriptService/Tests` from
+    being mapped a second time under `ServerScriptService`, so keep it.
+- **Save as UTF-8 without a BOM.** Rojo fails with `Failed to parse JSONC` on a file that starts
+  with a byte order mark. Windows PowerShell 5.1's `Set-Content` and `Out-File` add one, so save
+  from your editor. To check, run `head -c 3 default.project.json | od -An -tx1`: the output must
+  not be `ef bb bf`.
+- **Verify before you commit.** Run
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`. It must succeed,
+  and `sourcemap.json` should show the tree from the Layout table, including
+  `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages.Jest`. Then reconnect `rojo serve` and confirm the specs
+  still find their packages.
+- **Get a review** for any project-file change, even a one-liner.
